From dd88d02342c1748b5dd07ed78b180c533e44dd17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:22:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 259/333] Unified: preferences by what you want to set,
 effective at once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

☰ › Preferences (and the gear at the top right) opens six kinds: basic
(units, decimals, start page, FreeCAD's menus), mouse and keys (how the
mouse turns and moves the view, also for a touchpad; zoom at the cursor),
drawings (projection, decimals), files (DXF question, backups, recovery),
network and accounts (the network and AI key pages as they are), and the
AI. A change takes effect at once; "All preferences…" opens FreeCAD's
full preferences. A search field goes to the kind that has the words
(proxy, JIS, touchpad). The AI panel no longer always shows "run without
asking": it is under Preferences › AI (still only until FreeCAD closes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
